+patch: n/a
+---
+
+# PLAN-012: Pause/resume for session WAV recording
+
+## Status
+
+draft
+
+## Context
+
+The task asks that pausing a session also pause its WAV recording: no
+audio appended while paused, resume keeps writing to the same file, the
+file stays valid, non-recording sessions are unaffected, and automated
+tests cover the behavior.
+
+Verification against the current tree (all 145 tests pass): `sendAudio`
+in `server/session/manager.ts` already returns early when
+`active.paused`, so paused PCM never reaches `WavRecorder.append`, and
+the existing `session audio recording` test in `server/app.test.ts`
+asserts exactly that drop. The reported "recording keeps going" symptom
+does not reproduce here. What is missing is that the no-append-during-
+pause invariant lives only at that one call site: `WavRecorder` itself
+has no notion of pause, so any present or future `append` path that does
+not flow through the `active.paused` early-return (or a regression that
+moves/removes the check) silently records paused audio. There is also no
+dedicated test for the pause/resume recording contract; the only
+coverage is one inline assertion inside a larger test.
+
+This plan moves the invariant into the class that owns the file:
+`WavRecorder` gains explicit `pause()`/`resume()`, `SessionManager`
+drives them on session pause/resume, and dedicated tests pin the
+contract at both unit and end-to-end level. Observable behavior is
+intended to be identical to today; the change makes the guarantee
+structural instead of incidental.
+
+## Governing records
+
+- BDR-006: session audio is retained as a sibling `.wav` (default on) in
+  the `<stem>.md` / `<stem>.srt` / `<stem>.wav` bundle. This plan keeps
+  the single-file bundle contract: resume continues the same `.wav`, no
+  second artifact is created.
+- ADR-007: `.srt` cue timestamps are session/WAV-relative
+  (`streamBaseS`-shifted, paused wall time excluded). For cue times to
+  keep matching audio positions, paused time must produce zero WAV
+  bytes. That fixes the semantic choice: paused audio is dropped, not
+  replaced with silence.
+- ADR-001: the backend owns the filesystem artifacts; the fix lives in
+  `server/` (recorder + manager). The web client already tears down
+  capture on pause and drops nothing it still owes the server; stray
+  in-flight chunks are handled server-side as today.
+- ADR-006 / BDR-002: no new dependencies; the change is a boolean flag
+  plus tests.
+
+## Scope
+
+In scope:
+
+1. `server/audio/wav-recorder.ts`: `pause()` / `resume()` methods on
+   `WavRecorder`, dropping `append` calls submitted while paused.
+2. `server/session/manager.ts`: call `recorder.pause()` /
+   `recorder.resume()` from the session `pause()` / `resume()` paths.
+3. Automated tests: `server/audio/wav-recorder.test.ts` (unit) and
+   `server/app.test.ts` (end-to-end pause/resume recording cases).
+
+Out of scope:
+
+- Client changes (`web/`): capture pause already stops chunk production;
+  server-side drop covers anything still in flight.
+- Inserting silence or a gap marker into the WAV for the paused window
+  (rejected: breaks the ADR-007 cue-time alignment and adds nothing a
+  player needs - contiguous PCM is the correct artifact).
+- Incremental header patching so an unfinalized WAV reports a nonzero
+  duration (pre-existing limitation noted in PLAN-010 Risks).
+- Changes to `SessionInfo`, REST schemas, or socket events: pause state
+  is already broadcast via `session` events; recording pause needs no
+  new surface.
+
+## Contracts (literal)
+
+`server/audio/wav-recorder.ts` gains:
+
+```ts
+// WavRecorder
+pause(): void;    // appends submitted from now on are dropped; idempotent
+resume(): void;   // appends resume landing in the same file; idempotent
+get isPaused(): boolean; // observable state, used by tests
+```
+
+Pinned semantics:
+
+- `pause()` / `resume()` are synchronous flag flips on a private
+  `paused` field; they never touch the write queue, the fd, or the file.
+- `append(chunk)` checks `paused` at CALL time, before enqueueing:
+  `if (this.paused) return Promise.resolve();`. Checking at call time
+  (not inside the queued op) is a deliberate ordering decision: writes
+  already queued when `pause()` runs still complete, because those bytes
+  were captured before the pause. Anything submitted after the flag
+  flips is paused audio and is dropped. The single-threaded event loop
+  makes the flag boundary exact.
+- `bytesWritten` counts only bytes actually written; dropped appends
+  leave it unchanged.
+- `finalize()` and `abort()` are pause-agnostic: stop-while-paused must
+  still patch the header and close (existing `stop while paused ends the
+  session normally` flow). `done` keeps appends no-ops after finalize.
+- `isPaused` exists so tests assert state without reaching into private
+  fields; the manager does not consume it.
+
+`server/session/manager.ts` wiring:
+
+- `pause()`: after `active.paused = true; active.pausedAtMs = ...;
+  active.info.paused = true;` add `active.recorder?.pause();` (before
+  `stream.close()`; the recorder flag flip is synchronous and cheap).
+- `resume()`: after `active.stream = await this.openStream(active)` and
+  the paused fields flip to false, add `active.recorder?.resume();`.
+  Placement matters: if `openStream` throws, the session stays paused
+  and the recorder must stay paused too, so resume() on the recorder
+  runs only after the stream is confirmed open.
+- `sendAudio` keeps its `if (!active || active.paused) return;` early
+  return unchanged: it still guards the provider `send_audio` call,
+  which the recorder flag cannot. The two checks are intentional
+  redundancy - the manager gate protects the STT stream, the recorder
+  flag protects the file.
+- `recorder` stays `WavRecorder | null`; `?.` makes the non-recording
+  path a no-op by construction (requirement: pausing a non-recording
+  session is unaffected).
+
+## Steps
+
+### Step 1 - `server/audio/wav-recorder.ts`
+
+- Add `private paused = false;`, `pause()`, `resume()`, `get isPaused()`.
+- Gate `append` at call time per the pinned contract; the enqueued op
+  body (`!this.fh || this.done` guard, write, byte count) is unchanged.
+
+### Step 2 - `server/session/manager.ts`
+
+- Wire `active.recorder?.pause()` in `pause()` and
+  `active.recorder?.resume()` in `resume()` at the positions pinned
+  above. No new fields, no signature changes.
+
+### Step 3 - tests
+
+- Extend `server/audio/wav-recorder.test.ts` and `server/app.test.ts`
+  per the test plan below.
+
+## Test plan
+
+Automated (vitest), new cases:
+
+`server/audio/wav-recorder.test.ts`:
+
+- "drops appends while paused and resumes into the same file": create ->
+  `append(A)` -> `pause()` -> `append(B)` -> `resume()` -> `append(C)`
+  -> `finalize()`. Assert file payload equals `A` followed immediately
+  by `C` (contiguous, `B` absent), RIFF size `36 + |A| + |C|`, data size
+  `|A| + |C|`, `bytesWritten === |A| + |C|`.
+- "isPaused reflects pause/resume and both are idempotent": pause twice,
+  resume twice; `isPaused` true then false; appending between the double
+  pause still drops.
+- "finalize while paused still patches and closes": create -> append ->
+  `pause()` -> `finalize()` -> header sizes patched to the pre-pause
+  byte count; a later `append` resolves as a no-op (`done` guard).
+
+`server/app.test.ts` (inside `session audio recording` describe, reusing
+FakeProvider + `wavPathFor`):
+
+- "pauses and resumes the session WAV on pause/resume": start with
+  `recordAudio: true` -> send chunk A (known bytes) -> wait
+  `provider.audio` length 1 -> `POST /pause` -> stat the `.wav`: size is
+  `44 + |A|` after a settle delay AND stays `44 + |A|` after sending
+  chunk B while paused -> `POST /resume` -> send chunk C -> wait
+  `provider.audio` length 2 -> `POST /stop` -> read the file: data size
+  `|A| + |C|`, payload equals `A ++ C` contiguous, header sizes patched.
+  This asserts same-file resume (the `wx` flag makes a second file
+  impossible anyway) and byte-level absence of the paused chunk.
+- "stop while paused finalizes a valid WAV": start with
+  `recordAudio: true` -> send A -> `POST /pause` -> send B -> `POST
+  /stop` -> file parses as WAV, data size `|A|`, payload equals A.
+- "pause/resume on a non-recording session leaves no WAV": start without
+  `recordAudio` -> `POST /pause` -> send -> `POST /resume` -> `POST
+  /stop` -> `fs.access(wavPathFor(dir, id))` rejects.
+
+Existing tests that already touch this area and must keep passing: the
+paused-drop assertion inside "recordAudio tees sent PCM into a sibling
+.wav and serves it", the `pause/resume` describe block, and "keeps cue
+start cumulative across pause/resume".
+
+Gates: `npm test`, `npm run typecheck`.
+
+## Risks and notes
+
+- Assumption (recorded per task instruction): the reported live bug
+  ("recording keeps going") does not reproduce on this tree -
+  `sendAudio` already gates on `active.paused` and the suite is green.
+  The plan treats the task as making the guarantee structural in
+  `WavRecorder` plus dedicated coverage. If the reporter's build has the
+  tee before/outside the paused check, this same change fixes that
+  shape.
+- Dual flags (`active.paused` + `recorder.paused`) are intentional: they
+  protect different sinks (provider stream vs file). They cannot diverge
+  in current call paths because both flip synchronously inside the same
+  manager calls.
+- Call-time vs in-queue paused check: pinned call-time so pre-pause
+  bytes already queued still land; an in-queue check would drop a small
+  tail of legitimately-recorded audio on every pause.
+- "No gap or corruption" is interpreted as contiguous playable PCM with
+  a correctly patched header, not as an audible gap of silence - the
+  latter would desync ADR-007 cue timestamps from playback position.
+- Follow-up (unchanged by this plan): a crash or a never-finalized
+  session leaves `dataSize: 0` in the header while bytes exist (PLAN-010
+  Risks); pause/resume does not make this better or worse.
+
+## Definition of Done
+
+- [ ] `WavRecorder` exposes `pause()`, `resume()`, `isPaused`; `append`
+  submitted while paused resolves without writing and without counting
+  toward `bytesWritten`.
+- [ ] `SessionManager.pause()` pauses the recorder;
+  `SessionManager.resume()` resumes it only after the new stream opens.
+- [ ] Resumed recording appends to the same `.wav`; the finalized file
+  is a valid PCM WAV whose data section is exactly the unpaused bytes,
+  contiguous.
+- [ ] Pause/resume on a non-recording session is a no-op for artifacts
+  (no `.wav` appears, no error).
+- [ ] New unit + end-to-end tests pass; `npm test` and
+  `npm run typecheck` are clean.
-- 
2.50.0


