+## 22:03 - Pause/resume support for session WAV recording
+
+**Scope:** server/audio, server/session | **Type:** Fix | **Commit:** d1f9948 @ work
+
+## Scope
+server/audio, server/session
+
+## Type
+Fix
+
+## Commit
+- **Hash:** d1f9948
+- **Repo:** work
+- **Message:** Implement PLAN-012: pause/resume for session WAV recording
+- **Author:** Satoshi Man <mrvuong.bitcoin@gmail.com>
+- **Date:** 2026-11-05 22:03:10 +0700
+
+## User request
+Implement PLAN-012: pausing a session must also pause its WAV recording; resume keeps writing to the same file; non-recording sessions unaffected; automated tests cover the behavior.
+
+## Reason
+The no-append-during-pause invariant previously lived only at the sendAudio call site; moving it into WavRecorder makes the guarantee structural so future append paths or regressions cannot silently record paused audio. Per ADR-007, paused time must produce zero WAV bytes (drop, not silence) to keep cue timestamps aligned.
+
+## Description
+WavRecorder gained pause()/resume()/isPaused; append() drops chunks submitted while paused at call time so queued pre-pause bytes still land. SessionManager.pause()/resume() drive the recorder flag (resume only after the new STT stream opens). Added 3 unit tests in wav-recorder.test.ts and 3 end-to-end cases in app.test.ts covering same-file resume, stop-while-paused finalize, and non-recording sessions. PLAN-012 marked implemented with all DoD items checked.
+
+## Files changed
+CONTEXTS/03-implement-plan/PLAN-012-pause-resume-wav-recording.md
+server/app.test.ts
+server/audio/wav-recorder.test.ts
+server/audio/wav-recorder.ts
+server/session/manager.ts
+
+## Notes
+151 tests pass, tsc clean. Pre-existing flaky ms-level cue assertion in 'full session lifecycle' is unrelated (PLAN-012 Risks). Follow-up: unfinalized WAV headers still report dataSize 0 (PLAN-010 Risks).
+
+---
