+---
+id: PLAN-014-recording-status-ui
+status: draft
+date: 2026-11-05
+review_count: 0
+patch: n/a
+---
+
+# PLAN-014: Surface recording status and errors in the UI
+
+## Status
+
+draft
+
+## Context
+
+Session WAV recording (PLAN-010) is best-effort: `WavRecorder.create`
+failure rejects the session start, mid-session `append` failures set
+`recorderFailed` and only `log.warn`, and `finalize` failures in
+`finish()` only `log.error`. On the web side, `Live.tsx` renders a
+static `rec` badge whenever `state.active.record_audio` is true - the
+flag captured at start, not the recorder's real state.
+
+The result: while recording runs the user sees a static badge; when the
+recorder dies mid-session the badge keeps showing `rec` while nothing is
+being written; a create failure does reach the UI as a toast but with a
+raw fs message (`EEXIST: ...`), and a finalize failure is completely
+invisible.
+
+This plan makes the indicator reflect the real recorder state
+(`recording` / `paused` / `failed` / `off`) by adding a derived
+`recording` field to `SessionInfo`, and surfaces every recorder failure
+to the user through the existing `error` WS event -> sonner toast path.
+
+## Governing records
+
+- BDR-006 (supersedes BDR-005): session audio is retained by default as
+  a sibling WAV. Because retention is the default, its state is
+  first-class UI information - a silent failure violates the expectation
+  the default creates.
+- BDR-002 / ADR-006: no new dependencies. The indicator reuses `Badge`,
+  `LiveDot` (`animate-pulse-soft`), lucide icons, and sonner toasts.
+- ADR-001: server owns recording; state reaches the browser through the
+  `session` WS broadcast and the REST `SessionInfo` payload. The fix is
+  a state field on `SessionInfo`, not a new channel.
+- ADR-002: STT streaming is the paid resource; a recorder failure must
+  not interrupt transcription. Recording stays best-effort - only its
+  visibility changes.
+- PLAN-003 (UI design language): status semantics are pinned as
+  "live/recording = `--primary` pulsing dot" and destructive is the
+  error color. The indicator follows those exact rules.
+- PLAN-010: recording semantics are unchanged - create failure fails the
+  start (the user asked for recording, so failing is more honest than
+  silently running unrecorded), mid-session failure continues the
+  session unrecorded with at most one notification. This plan changes
+  only where the failure is *seen*, not whether the session survives.
+- PLAN-012: pause/resume semantics preserved - paused audio never
+  reaches the write queue, so 'paused' is a recording state too, not
+  just a session state.
+
+## Scope
+
+In scope:
+
+1. `server/session/manager.ts`: `RecordingState` type + `recording`
+   field on `SessionInfo`, a `RecordingUnavailableError`, a
+   `recorderFactory` test seam on `SessionManagerDeps`, an
+   `error`-event + `session` rebroadcast on mid-session append failure,
+   and an `error` event on finalize failure.
+2. `web/src/lib/types.ts`: mirror `RecordingState` and the new field.
+3. `web/src/pages/Live.tsx`: replace the static `rec` badge with a
+   state-driven indicator (`rec` pulsing / `rec paused` / `rec failed`).
+4. `server/app.test.ts`: new tests under `session audio recording`.
+
+Out of scope:
+
+- Retry/recovery of a failed recorder. `failed` is terminal for the
+  session, matching the existing `recorderFailed` semantics.
+- Surfacing recording state on the Review page or Sessions list
+  (post-session artifacts are unchanged).
+- Toaster/error-plumbing changes: `handleEvent`'s `'error'` case already
+  toasts, and `start()`'s catch already toasts REST failures.
+- Changing `record_audio` semantics or removing it (kept for
+  compatibility; see Contracts).
+- Changes to `WavRecorder` itself, `routes.ts`, `ws.ts`,
+  `use-live-session.ts`, or the PiP transcript.
+
+## Contracts (literal)
+
+### `server/session/manager.ts`
+
+```ts
+export type RecordingState = 'off' | 'recording' | 'paused' | 'failed';
+```
+
+`SessionInfo` gains one field:
+
+```ts
+export interface SessionInfo {
+  // ...existing fields unchanged...
+  paused: boolean;
+  assist: boolean;
+  record_audio: boolean;
+  recording: RecordingState;
+}
+```
+
+`record_audio` keeps its current meaning ("recording was enabled for
+this session") so existing tests and payloads are undisturbed;
+`recording` is the state the UI renders.
+
+```ts
+export class RecordingUnavailableError extends Error {
+  readonly code = 'RECORDING_UNAVAILABLE';
+}
+```
+
+- Constructed in `start()` around `WavRecorder.create`; message shape
+  (pinned): `` `session audio could not be recorded: ${causeMessage}` ``
+  where `causeMessage` is `cause instanceof Error ? cause.message :
+  String(cause)`.
+- It is not mapped in `setErrorHandler`, so it returns the generic 500
+  `{ error, code }` body. The client's `start()` catch already toasts
+  `body.error`, which is the required clear notification.
+
+```ts
+// SessionManagerDeps gains a test seam, same pattern as providerFactory:
+recorderFactory?: (filePath: string, opts: WavRecorderOptions) => Promise<WavRecorder>;
+```
+
+- Resolved in the constructor as
+  `deps.recorderFactory ?? ((p, o) => WavRecorder.create(p, o))` and
+  called in `start()` where `WavRecorder.create` is called today.
+
+State machine (the field lives on `active.info` and is mutated wherever
+`info.paused` is already mutated, so every `session` broadcast and every
+`GET /api/sessions` response carries the live value - including the
+initial `session` event a reconnecting socket receives):
+
+| Transition | Rule |
+|---|---|
+| `start()` | `recording = recorder != null ? 'recording' : 'off'` |
+| `pause()` | `if (info.recording === 'recording') info.recording = 'paused'` |
+| `resume()` | `if (info.recording === 'paused') info.recording = 'recording'` |
+| append failure | `info.recording = 'failed'` (see below) |
+| `finish()` | no change - the session ends; idle carries no info |
+
+`failed` is sticky: a failed recorder that later pauses reports
+`failed`, not `paused`, because 'paused' would claim recording resumes
+on resume.
+
+Mid-session append failure (`sendAudio`'s `.catch`, inside the existing
+`recorderFailed` guard so it fires at most once), pinned order and text:
+
+```ts
+active.recorderFailed = true;
+active.info.recording = 'failed';
+this.broadcast({
+  type: 'error',
+  code: 'RECORDING_FAILED',
+  message: 'session audio recording failed; continuing without saving audio',
+});
+this.broadcast({ type: 'session', state: 'active', session: active.info });
+```
+
+Finalize failure (`finish()`'s `recorder.finalize()` catch), broadcast
+before the `session: idle` event so the notification precedes the
+session-ended navigation:
+
+```ts
+this.broadcast({
+  type: 'error',
+  code: 'RECORDING_FAILED',
+  message: 'session audio could not be finalized; the saved recording may be incomplete',
+});
+```
+
+The `error` `ServerEvent` variant already carries `code?: string` on
+both ends; no transport change.
+
+### `web/src/lib/types.ts`
+
+```ts
+export type RecordingState = 'off' | 'recording' | 'paused' | 'failed';
+
+// SessionInfo gains:
+recording: RecordingState;
+```
+
+### `web/src/pages/Live.tsx`
+
+The current block
+
+```tsx
+{state.active.record_audio ? (
+  <Badge variant="secondary">
+    <AudioLines data-icon="inline-start" />
+    rec
+  </Badge>
+) : null}
+```
+
+is replaced by (pinned literals; ordering in the badge row unchanged -
+it stays where `rec` sits today, after `lag` and before `assist`):
+
+```tsx
+{state.active.recording === 'recording' ? (
+  <Badge variant="secondary">
+    <LiveDot />
+    rec
+  </Badge>
+) : null}
+{state.active.recording === 'paused' ? (
+  <Badge variant="outline">
+    <Pause data-icon="inline-start" />
+    rec paused
+  </Badge>
+) : null}
+{state.active.recording === 'failed' ? (
+  <Badge variant="destructive">
+    <AudioLines data-icon="inline-start" />
+    rec failed
+  </Badge>
+) : null}
+```
+
+- `LiveDot` is imported from `@/components/transcript` (the
+  `animate-pulse-soft` primary dot PLAN-003 pins for live/recording).
+- `Pause` is added to the `lucide-react` import.
+- `recording === 'off'` renders nothing, matching today's hidden badge
+  when `record_audio` is false.
+- The existing standalone `paused` badge is untouched - the
+  "paused sessions show paused" requirement is covered both by it and by
+  `rec paused`.
+
+## Steps
+
+### Step 1 - `server/session/manager.ts`
+
+- Add `RecordingState`, the `recording` field on `SessionInfo`, and
+  `RecordingUnavailableError` per the contract.
+- Add `recorderFactory` to `SessionManagerDeps`; resolve it in the
+  constructor next to the other factories.
+- In `start()`: wrap the factory call so a rejection throws
+  `RecordingUnavailableError`; initialize `info.recording`.
+- In `sendAudio()`: extend the existing append `.catch` to set
+  `info.recording = 'failed'` and broadcast the pinned `error` +
+  `session` events.
+- In `pause()` / `resume()`: apply the state-machine transitions next to
+  the existing `info.paused` flips.
+- In `finish()`: broadcast the pinned finalize-failure `error` before
+  the existing `session: idle` broadcast.
+
+### Step 2 - `web/src/lib/types.ts`
+
+- Add `RecordingState` and the `recording` field to `SessionInfo`.
+
+### Step 3 - `web/src/pages/Live.tsx`
+
+- Swap the badge block per the contract; add the `Pause` and `LiveDot`
+  imports.
+
+### Step 4 - tests
+
+- Extend `server/app.test.ts` per the test plan.
+
+## Test plan
+
+Automated (vitest), new cases in the `session audio recording`
+describe of `server/app.test.ts`. Failures are injected through
+`deps.recorderFactory`, which `beforeEach` already exposes via the
+shared `deps` object; a failing stub is cast `as WavRecorder` like the
+existing translator/assistant stubs.
+
+- "reports recording state on the session surface": start with
+  `recordAudio: true` - the POST response carries
+  `recording: 'recording'`; a fresh WS client's first `session` event
+  carries `session.recording === 'recording'`; after `POST /pause` the
+  last active `session` event carries `'paused'`; after `POST /resume`
+  it carries `'recording'` again. A second case starts without
+  `recordAudio` and asserts `recording === 'off'`.
+- "rejects the start when the WAV cannot be created":
+  `deps.recorderFactory = async () => { throw new Error('EEXIST: file exists') }`;
+  `POST /api/sessions` with `recordAudio: true` returns 500,
+  `body.code === 'RECORDING_UNAVAILABLE'`, and `body.error` contains
+  `session audio could not be recorded`; `GET /api/sessions` shows
+  `active === null`.
+- "surfaces a mid-session recording failure once": `deps.recorderFactory`
+  resolves to a stub whose `append` always rejects; start with
+  `recordAudio: true`, connect WS, send two PCM chunks - `vi.waitFor`
+  an `error` event with `code === 'RECORDING_FAILED'` and a `session`
+  active event with `session.recording === 'failed'`; send a third
+  chunk and assert (after a settle wait) exactly one
+  `RECORDING_FAILED` error total, that the provider still received all
+  chunks (session continues unrecorded), and that stop succeeds.
+- "notifies when the recording cannot be finalized": stub with a
+  working `append` and a rejecting `finalize`; start, stop, then assert
+  the `RECORDING_FAILED` `error` event appears in `messages` before the
+  `session: idle` event.
+
+Existing tests that must keep passing: the whole `session audio
+recording`, `pause/resume`, and `REST + WS surface` describes (the new
+field is additive). `web/src/lib/use-live-session.test.ts` needs no
+changes - the reducer stores `SessionInfo` verbatim.
+
+Gates: `npm test`, `npm run typecheck`. Note: root `tsc --noEmit`
+covers `server/` only; the `web/` edit is verified by
+`npm --prefix web run build` (`tsc -b && vite build`) plus a manual
+`npm run dev` smoke check of the badge states.
+
+## Risks and notes
+
+- Assumption (recorded per task instruction): "recording unavailable"
+  keeps the PLAN-010 semantics - the session start fails rather than
+  running unrecorded - and "a clear error notification" is the existing
+  `toast.error(body.error)` path; this plan only makes the message
+  explicit (`session audio could not be recorded: <cause>`) instead of
+  a bare fs error.
+- Assumption: "stopped sessions stop showing it" is satisfied by the
+  existing flow - the `session: idle` broadcast clears `state.active`,
+  unmounting the whole status bar; no persisted 'stopped' state is
+  added.
+- Assumption: `record_audio` stays on `SessionInfo` even though
+  `recording !== 'off'` encodes the same fact; existing tests assert it
+  and the start-form contract is unchanged. A later cleanup could
+  deprecate it.
+- `recording` is additive on `SessionInfo`; an older server would send
+  no field and the client would render no badge (same as
+  `record_audio: false`). Single-binary app ships both ends together.
+- The PiP transcript (`PipTranscript`) has no badge row; the indicator
+  lives in the page status bar only, same as the current `rec` badge.
+- `failed` while paused: pinned as 'failed' (sticky), so resume does not
+  falsely promise recording will come back; transcription itself is
+  unaffected either way.
+- The finalize-failure toast may race `onSessionEnded` navigation to
+  Review; sonner toasts persist across client-side navigation and the
+  error event is pinned before `idle`, so it is still seen.
+- Pre-existing flake carried over from earlier plans: `REST + WS
+  surface > full session lifecycle` asserts exact millisecond cue times
+  that can drift by 1 ms; re-run before treating the gate as failed.
+
+## Definition of Done
+
+- [ ] `SessionInfo` carries `recording: 'off' | 'recording' | 'paused' |
+      'failed'` end-to-end (server type, WS events, REST payloads, web
+      type), and `record_audio` is unchanged.
+- [ ] `recording` tracks real state: `'recording'` only while the
+      recorder accepts appends, `'paused'` while the session is paused
+      with an intact recorder, `'failed'` after any append failure, and
+      no badge/state when recording is off or the session has ended.
+- [ ] A mid-session append failure produces exactly one
+      `RECORDING_FAILED` `error` event (toast-visible) plus a `session`
+      rebroadcast carrying `recording: 'failed'`; the transcription
+      session continues.
+- [ ] A `finalize` failure produces a `RECORDING_FAILED` `error` event
+      broadcast before `session: idle`.
+- [ ] A `WavRecorder.create` failure rejects `POST /api/sessions` with
+      `code: 'RECORDING_UNAVAILABLE'` and a message starting
+      `session audio could not be recorded:`; no session is left
+      running.
+- [ ] `SessionManagerDeps.recorderFactory` exists and defaults to
+      `WavRecorder.create`.
+- [ ] Live.tsx renders `rec` (pulsing `LiveDot`, secondary), `rec
+      paused` (outline + Pause icon), `rec failed` (destructive), or
+      nothing, keyed on `state.active.recording`.
+- [ ] New `app.test.ts` cases pass; `npm test` and `npm run typecheck`
+      are clean.
